From 472bc8447c58c0b41d1111af33af634bb6e64503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:48:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show a 3D video to the compositor as stereo content

Under a compositor that takes stereo content declarations (kde_stereo_content_v1,
with wl_subcompositor, wp_viewporter and wl_shm), the video of a stereoscopic 3D
file is drawn into a surface of its own under the window's surface, both views
side by side at the size of one view, the left eye first, and declared as full
side by side. The controls stay in the window's surface over it, the same in both
eyes, and what the layer does not cover is black. Qt creates subsurfaces only
above their parent, so the layer is a wl_subsurface made here.

The 3D Video menu gets a 3D entry (the default where the layer is supported) and
Display Settings, which opens the screen's settings where its 3D mode is chosen.
Everywhere else Dragon Player works as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
